   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "6  Theory: the ideas behind each step",
   "originalText": "6  Theory: the ideas behind each step",
   "fontSize": 28,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "rectangle-133",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1760,
   "width": 547,
   "height": 340,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
   "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   },
   "seed": 1468909588,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1050670470,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "id": "text-134"
    }
   ],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false
  },
  {
   "id": "text-134",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 48,
   "y": 1817.5,
   "width": 505.44,
   "height": 225.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1122348329,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 248391022,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "WHAT IS AN LLM\n\nA neural network trained on huge amounts of text.\nGiven some text, it predicts the next token, again and\nagain, and that is how it writes. It has no live\ndatabase, so it does not know today's price or stock,\nand its knowledge stops at a training cutoff. It can\nsound confident while being wrong, which is called\nhallucination. Treat it as a writer and reasoner, not\na source of truth.",
   "originalText": "WHAT IS AN LLM\n\nA neural network trained on huge amounts of text.\nGiven some text, it predicts the next token, again and\nagain, and that is how it writes. It has no live\ndatabase, so it does not know today's price or stock,\nand its knowledge stops at a training cutoff. It can\nsound confident while being wrong, which is called\nhallucination. Treat it as a writer and reasoner, not\na source of truth.",
   "fontSize": 18,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "rectangle-133",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "rectangle-135",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 608,
   "y": 1760,
   "width": 547,
   "height": 340,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
   "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   },
   "seed": 600369833,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 716836975,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "id": "text-136"
    }
   ],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false
  },
  {
   "id": "text-136",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 626,
   "y": 1828.75,
   "width": 486.72,
   "height": 202.5,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 460349300,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 786490146,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "TOKENS AND CONTEXT WINDOW\n\nText is split into tokens, small pieces of words.\nEverything in one call (system prompt, chat history,\nretrieved evidence and the answer) must fit in the\ncontext window. APIs usually charge per input and\noutput token, so more context costs more and can be\nslower. The model remembers nothing between calls:\nyour app resends whatever history it needs.",
   "originalText": "TOKENS AND CONTEXT WINDOW\n\nText is split into tokens, small pieces of words.\nEverything in one call (system prompt, chat history,\nretrieved evidence and the answer) must fit in the\ncontext window. APIs usually charge per input and\noutput token, so more context costs more and can be\nslower. The model remembers nothing between calls:\nyour app resends whatever history it needs.",
   "fontSize": 18,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "rectangle-135",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "rectangle-137",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 1186,
   "y": 1760,
   "width": 547,
   "height": 340,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
   "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   },
   "seed": 1015108052,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1162595516,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "id": "text-138"
    }
   ],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false
  },
  {
   "id": "text-138",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1204,
   "y": 1828.75,
   "width": 496.08000000000004,
   "height": 202.5,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 354580404,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 229990660,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "WHY RAG EXISTS\n\nThe model does not know your data, and retraining it\nfor every price change is impractical. RAG fetches\nrelevant facts at question time and puts them in the\nprompt. This gives fresher answers, fewer invented\nfacts, and answers that can point to a source. The\nlimit: if retrieval misses the right item, the answer\nfails too. So measure retrieval first, then the LLM.",
   "originalText": "WHY RAG EXISTS\n\nThe model does not know your data, and retraining it\nfor every price change is impractical. RAG fetches\nrelevant facts at question time and puts them in the\nprompt. This gives fresher answers, fewer invented\nfacts, and answers that can point to a source. The\nlimit: if retrieval misses the right item, the answer\nfails too. So measure retrieval first, then the LLM.",
   "fontSize": 18,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "rectangle-137",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "rectangle-139",
